@@ -3,3 +3,14 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns the value a JSON Pointer
+([RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901)) refers to. It throws an `Error` when the pointer
+is not valid (it must be empty or start with `/`, and `~` must be followed by `0` or `1`) or when it
+does not resolve: a missing member, an array index that is out of range, has a leading zero or is `-`
+(the nonexistent element after the last), or a scalar that is traversed. Only own members of objects
+are resolved, so `/__proto__` or `/toString` never reach inherited properties.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
